        "prompt": "Describe what is different between the two methods.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "In method 1, they divided first. In method 2, they expanded first. In this example, method 1 was faster because $15$ has a factor of $3$.",
          "worked": "Method 1 divides both sides by $3$, then subtracts $1$. Method 2 expands, subtracts $3$ from both sides, then divides by $3$. Both give $x=4$. Method 1 uses fewer steps here because $15$ is divisible by $3$.",
